Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5: disable handover_irq once handover completes

On SM8450 (`2400000.remoteproc` SLPI/SSC PAS), the remote subsystem toggles
its SMP2P handover state bit multiple times after boot handover has already
completed, triggering repeated wakeups and log spam (`Handover signaled,
but it already happened`).

Mask `handover_irq` via `disable_irq_nosync()` inside
`q6v5_handover_interrupt()` as soon as `handover_issued` becomes `true`, and
guard the `disable_irq(q6v5->handover_irq)` call in `qcom_q6v5_unprepare()`
with `if (!q6v5->handover_issued)` so IRQ disable depth stays balanced across
remoteproc stop/restart cycles (`qcom_q6v5_prepare()` re-enables it).

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
index 849ae26..31e8573 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
@@ -78,7 +78,8 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(qcom_q6v5_prepare);
  */
 int qcom_q6v5_unprepare(struct qcom_q6v5 *q6v5)
 {
-	disable_irq(q6v5->handover_irq);
+	if (!q6v5->handover_issued)
+		disable_irq(q6v5->handover_irq);
 	q6v5_load_state_toggle(q6v5, false);
 
 	/* Disable interconnect vote, in case handover never happened */
@@ -175,6 +176,7 @@ static irqreturn_t q6v5_handover_interrupt(int irq, void *data)
 	icc_set_bw(q6v5->path, 0, 0);
 
 	q6v5->handover_issued = true;
+	disable_irq_nosync(q6v5->handover_irq);
 
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 }
